      "schema_version": "aspr_gear",
      "text": "This study uses reconstituted β-galactosidase ribosome:nascent-chain complexes to show that GroEL can engage, locally destabilize, and partially encapsulate a nascent domain with GroES. The contribution is a cotranslational mechanism supported by complementary assays and chaperone-competition experiments. Its principal limits are unresolved active-complex topology, uncertain specificity and physiological significance of the ribosome interaction, and incomplete mechanistic separation of direct local unfolding, entropic pulling, and chaperone competition."
    },
